      "title": "Unemployment Rate",
      "description": "The percentage of people in the labor force who are actively looking for work but don't have a job. It's seasonally adjusted to remove predictable swings (like holiday hiring) so the underlying trend is clearer. Historically, anything under ~5% is considered healthy. Spikes - like the one in 2020 - signal economic shocks that ripple into wages, benefits, and job security. Even if you're employed, a rising unemployment rate usually means less leverage to negotiate raises or switch jobs.",
