      "id": 6,
      "title": "Shelter / Rent Index",
      "description": "The BLS shelter index measures the cost of housing over time - it covers rent paid by renters and an equivalent estimated rent for homeowners (called 'owners' equivalent rent'). Like the overall CPI, it's indexed to 100 in 1982-84. Shelter is typically the largest single expense in a household budget, and this index rising faster than wages is the clearest signal that housing affordability is getting worse. It tends to lag real-world rent changes by 6-12 months because leases are slow to turn over.",
