      "id": 8,
      "title": "California Gasoline Price (per gallon)",
      "description": "Weekly retail price for regular unleaded gasoline in California, reported every Monday by the Energy Information Administration. California consistently ranks among the most expensive states for gas due to its unique fuel blend requirements (CARB-reformulated gasoline reduces smog but costs more to produce), higher state and local taxes, and limited pipeline connections to refineries outside the state. Weekly data captures price swings much faster than the monthly BLS national average, so this panel shows what you are actually paying at the pump right now. Compare it to the national average panel above to see how much of a California premium you are carrying.",
