    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "California Electricity Price (per kWh)",
      "description": "Average retail price per kilowatthour paid by California residential customers, reported monthly by the EIA. California electricity prices are consistently among the highest in the continental U.S., driven by the state's aggressive renewable energy mandates, aging transmission infrastructure, and utility wildfire liability costs that get passed directly to ratepayers. This is the rate reflected on your PG&E, SCE, or SDG&E bill. Even if your usage stays flat, a rising price here means your bill quietly grows every year. The long-term upward slope on this chart is one of the clearest pictures of how energy policy translates into household expenses.",
