      "id": 12,
      "title": "30-Year Fixed Mortgage Rate",
      "description": "The interest rate on a 30-year fixed-rate home mortgage, surveyed weekly by Freddie Mac. This single number determines housing affordability more than any other — when it is low, the same monthly payment buys a far more expensive house; when it spikes, buyers get priced out and the market freezes. It tracks closely with the 10-year Treasury yield, which in turn responds to Fed policy and inflation expectations. The near-zero rates of 2020-2021 supercharged home prices by making borrowing almost free. The rapid rise to 7-8% in 2022-2023 was the fastest affordability shock in modern history, effectively locking millions of existing homeowners in place because selling meant giving up a 3% rate for a 7% one.",
